From dab0eac7d725abbd75f4a8ea659538d7a69a5136 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guild-Idler Patch Tool <patch@guild-idler.local>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 02:15:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0188: Quest chain narrative consistency pass

Direct review flagged Crow's Warning not holding together end to end
(cure sent to an unconnected location) and Third Crown's description
contradicting itself (a lord who did not come from a noble house).
Broadened into a full re-check of all 29 chains for the same two
failure modes: collapsed clauses creating false contradictions, and
threats never actually named in their own chain's description or
epilogue.

Fixes:
- third_crown: corrected the toll/manor distinction
- crows_warning: fixed cure's destination (Greywick then Thornhollow,
  not IronRest), named the transformation (ghouls)
- millers_problem, what_the_culled_become, hollow_choir,
  full_moon_over_ashvale, body_snatcher_problem, hunt_a_lich: named
  the antagonist where it was previously only 'something'/'whatever'
- something_big_in_the_foothills: named hill giants consistently
  (previously only a stray 'ogres' aside in the epilogue)
- ancient_crown, lost_kingdom: invented concrete guardians (empty
  armor, living stone construct) for previously-unnamed non-combat
  guarding presences

Explicitly left alone: the_last_clutch (threat never fought),
last_pilgrimage and quiet_in_millbrook (intentional, both continue
into later content).

One stage rename: crows_warning's 4th stage, to match its corrected
destination. No other mechanical fields touched.
